Small spoilers...

OK, so I'm sitting on DLvl 1 and ELvl 1, when a trunk grants
me a genocide scroll (I didn't know it was genocide at the time).
Not having an altar around to test its' cursed/blessed status, I
read it anyway. So, I'm thinking, as it is waiting for a monster
name (ahah!, it's not blessed), if it's cursed, I don't want to end
up with a bunch of master liches around with me with only a
+0 leather armor, +0 fedora, and a +2 bullwhip (archeologist).

So, I'm thinking to myself, "What character can I genocide that
will be good to have gone if its' uncursed, while at the same
time I can handle as a lvl 1 character?" Well, I chose a rust
monster and it turned out to be cursed. I get 5 rust monsters.

Since I have leather armor, a fedora, and a bullwhip, I don't
have to worry about rusting, and a rust monsters' touch attack
doesn't hurt, I backed myself into a closet and started to wail
away at the monsters. Get this... for every one of the rust
monsters I killed, I gained one experience level. Knight the dog
killed one of them, so I left the closet ELvl 5. So, the next thing
that came across my path was a jackal, and killing it gave me
ELvl 6. Incredible!

Hell, from now on, I'm going to reverse genocide rust monsters
instead of wraiths if they give me that kind of benefit. I don't
even have to satiate myself on the corpses to get the level gain.
(This is somewhat tongue in cheek, I normally don't bother
genociding rust monsters because by the time they are around in
large enough numbers to be bothersome, I have rustproof armor
and weapons).

So, if you ever find yourself in the same situation, feel free to
go after rust monsters.

BTW, this game ended sadly when Clive the Archeologist stepped
on a sleeping gas trap and was mauled by a boneslevel kitten.
Argh!
